  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 315 AM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nThe front should be through the region with northwesterly flow\nin place by Tuesday, and it will be considerably cooler as a\nresult. Highs Tuesday-Friday will be in the upper 70s to near 80\nnear the Arkansas/Missouri border, and in the low to mid-70s\nnorth into central Missouri. Overnight lows will even drop into\nthe mid- to low 50s on Tuesday and Wednesday nights, with the\nlower terrain in the eastern Ozarks likely to drop below 50\ndegrees overnight this week! The air mass that settles in behind\nthe front won't be overly dry either, which should prevent\nafternoon RHs from dropping below 40% in the afternoons most\ndays this week as well.\n\nRidging aloft will build back across the Southern Plains after \nthe frontal passage early in the week, but our region should\ngenerally remain in northerly flow with the heart of the ridge \nto our southwest. This should keep temperatures stable through \nthe week, rather than the warming trend we often see when\nridging puts us in southwesterly flow. However, this does mean\nthere is a signal that we will remain dry through at least the \nend of the work week, which will support further worsening of\ndrought conditions.",
